This is a tool-gated math task. Complete the mandatory external workflow before doing any math reasoning.

Your first assistant response must contain exactly one bash tool call and no math reasoning, no explanation, and no Answer line. Continue with exactly one bash tool call per assistant response until the workflow is complete.

This session requires exactly 4 sequential bash tool call(s), producing an expected total of 5 model steps including the final answer.

Tool workflow:
1. In one bash tool call, run exactly `printf '%s\n' 'c0b36aca9edac8dd0fba9f3bc1b4a7011f70a7c6282daf77fbbf6d8b225987cb' > /tmp/dressage-chain-c0b36aca9edac8dd-00`. This creates the workflow state file.
2. Only after the previous result is available, make one new bash tool call and run exactly `sha256sum /tmp/dressage-chain-c0b36aca9edac8dd-00 > /tmp/dressage-chain-c0b36aca9edac8dd-01`.
3. Only after the previous result is available, make one new bash tool call and run exactly `sha256sum /tmp/dressage-chain-c0b36aca9edac8dd-01 > /tmp/dressage-chain-c0b36aca9edac8dd-02`.
4. Only after the previous result is available, make one new bash tool call and run exactly `cat /tmp/dressage-chain-c0b36aca9edac8dd-02`. Remember the first eight hexadecimal characters printed by this command as <CODE>.

Workflow rules:
- Wait for each tool result before deciding and issuing the next tool call.
- Do not issue parallel tool calls.
- Do not combine workflow commands with `;`, `&&`, pipelines, or scripts.
- Do not skip, reorder, or add tool calls.
- After all required tool calls finish, make no more tool calls.
- Only after the final tool result is available, solve the math problem below.
- The last line of your response should still be of the form Answer: \boxed{$Answer}. Also mention Workflow code: <CODE> before the last line.

Math problem:
The last line of your response should be of the form Answer: \boxed{$Answer} where $Answer is the answer to the problem.

What is the ratio of the area of the shaded square to the area of the large square? (The figure is drawn to scale.) [asy]
/* AMC8 1998 #13P */
size(1inch,1inch);
pair r1c1=(0,0), r1c2=(10,0), r1c3=(20,0), r1c4=(30, 0), r1c5=(40, 0);
pair r2c1=(0,10), r2c2=(10,10), r2c3=(20,10), r2c4=(30, 10), r2c5=(40, 10);
pair r3c1=(0,20), r3c2=(10,20), r3c3=(20,20), r3c4=(30, 20), r3c5=(40, 20);
pair r4c1=(0,30), r4c2=(10,30), r4c3=(20,30), r4c4=(30, 30), r4c5=(40, 30);
pair r5c1=(0,40), r5c2=(10,40), r5c3=(20,40), r5c4=(30, 40), r5c5=(40, 40);
draw(r1c1--r5c1--r5c5--r1c5--r1c1--r5c5);
draw(r5c1--r3c3);
draw(r4c4--r2c4--r3c5);
fill(r2c2--r3c3--r2c4--r1c3--cycle);
[/asy]The answer is in the form \frac{m}{n}, where gcd(m, n) = 1. Please provide the value of m + n.

Remember to put your answer on its own line after "Answer:".
